Aureus Arena — Licensing
========================

This repository uses a dual-licensing model:

## Solana Program (program/)

Licensed under the Business Source License 1.1 (BSL 1.1).

- You may view, audit, copy, modify, and make non-production use of the code.
- You may NOT deploy a modified or unmodified copy as a competing on-chain
  program on any blockchain without a commercial license.
- On February 25, 2028 (the Change Date), the license automatically converts
  to the MIT License.

See program/LICENSE for the full BSL 1.1 text.

## Everything Else (sdk/, frontend/, examples/, mcp-server/, client/)

Licensed under the MIT License.

See LICENSE-MIT for the full MIT text.

---

This model mirrors the approach used by Uniswap v3, Aave v3, and other
leading DeFi protocols: the core protocol is source-available with time-
delayed open-source conversion, while all tooling and interfaces are
fully open source from day one.
